
# Snowflake Cortex Sentiment — Project Notes

## What this is
Point-in-time sentiment scoring of Amazon Best Sellers reviews
using Snowflake Cortex AI. No Python ML. No external tools. Pure SQL + Streamlit.

## Stack
- Source: Amazon Best Sellers dataset (Snowflake Marketplace)
- Scoring: SNOWFLAKE.CORTEX.SENTIMENT(BODY)
- Storage: Static CTAS table — sentiment_lab.analytics.review_sentiment
- Dashboard: Streamlit in Snowflake (SiS)
- Charts: Altair

## Why Dynamic Table not used
Marketplace listings = read-only. Can't set as DT source.
Workaround: CTAS snapshot. Re-run to refresh.

## Next ideas
- [ ] Schedule CTAS refresh via Snowflake Task
- [ ] Add CORTEX.SUMMARIZE() for negative review grouping
- [ ] Swap to Dynamic Table once data lands in own schema
- [ ] Add product category breakdown if column available
- [ ] Cortex score vs star rating validation

## Cortex thresholds used
> +0.3 = POSITIVE
< -0.3 = NEGATIVE
else   = NEUTRAL

## Lessons learned
- Altair v6 no nested alt.condition() — push colour logic to SQL
- Dynamic Tables need owned tables, not marketplace shares
